  "query_preview": "..\nA broad upper trough over the Gulf of Alaska will allow storm\nsystems to crash into British Columbia over the next several days\nwith drier/weaker systems emerging lee of the Rockies.\n\nThis pattern brings mild and dry conditions with an increase in \nwinds with any dry fronts that pass through. Winds this afternoon \nare expected to become calm tonight but begin increase from the \nSE Sunday then turn to the W late in the day. Highest winds look \nto be near the Canadian border so no Wind products will be issued \nwith this package.\n\nRidging builds back into the Pacific Northwest Tuesday night and\nexpands throughout the week. This should keep conditions dry \nthrough the end of the work week but ensembles amplify this ridge \nheavily into Friday. Afterward confidence goes to low as ensemble \ngroups disagree on how to break the ridge down. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nDid blend Winds Sunday afternoon and night with the NBM90. The\nremainder of the forecast was left alone. TFJ",
